  "_README": [
    "This is a TEMPLATE. Do not commit a real client config here.",
    "",
    "How to get the real file (operator one-time setup, ~20 minutes):",
    "  1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create a project named 'Mnemify'.",
    "  2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable each Google API you'll harvest:",
    "     - Gmail API (for the gmail source)",
    "     - Google Drive API (later)",
    "     - Google Calendar API (later)",
    "     - Google Docs API (later)",
    "     One project hosts all of them.",
    "  3. APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen -> External user type.",
    "     Fill in: app name 'Mnemify', user support email, developer contact email.",
    "     Add the scopes you'll use:",
    "       https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.readonly",
    "       https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly  (later)",
    "       https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly  (later)",
    "  4. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials ->",
    "     OAuth client ID -> Application type: Desktop app -> name 'Mnemify Desktop'.",
    "     Click Download JSON.",
    "  5. Rename the downloaded file to oauth_client.json and drop it in this directory",
    "     (alongside this .template file). The .gitignore keeps it out of git.",
    "  6. Verify locally: `mnemify login --source gmail` opens a browser,",
    "     you click Allow, and the refresh token is cached at",
    "     ~/.mnemify/google/gmail-token.json (mode 0600).",
    "  7. Before public launch: APIs & Services -> OAuth consent screen ->",
    "     Publish App -> Submit for verification. The 'gmail.readonly' scope is a",
    "     restricted scope; verification removes the 'Google hasn't verified this app'",
    "     warning users see today. Typically 4-6 weeks; needs a privacy policy URL,",
    "     a demo video, and a security questionnaire.",
    "",
    "Until you drop in the real file, every Google-source plugin will raise",
    "EnvironmentError at factory time with a pointer back here."
